VALUES (778, 'tt0046487', NULL, 'Monsieur Hulot''s Holiday', 'Les vacances de Monsieur Hulot', 'movie', 1953, 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/r4F4tsU0Ajeh9ZYUkWOJSYmioj7.jpg', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/dK6s1EMpMcUwBHpiYVMBiTdgdvy.jpg', 'Monsieur Hulot, Jacques Tati’s endearing clown, takes a holiday at a seaside resort, where his presence provokes one catastrophe after another. Tati’s masterpiece of gentle slapstick is a series of effortlessly well-choreographed sight gags involving dogs, boats, and firecrackers; it was the first entry in the Hulot series and the film that launched its maker to international stardom.', NULL, NULL, 2.4257, 6.951, 0, 7.69333333333333335e+00, '2026-07-15 12:01:52', '2026-11-20 00:55:15')
